From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] editor: smooth value noise for the noise brush
 (ed_terrain_brush noise settings), ed_tt_disc / ed_tt_nodes for the terrain
 type brush and overlay

ed_terrain_brush takes three optional trailing arguments (noiseScale, noiseOctaves, noiseRoughness). The noise mode is now smooth value noise on a lattice
(seeded integer hash, intermediates below 2^24, smoothstep blend, up to 4 octaves) sampled at the world position, so it is continuous across the dabs of a
stroke; EdBrush.h and terrain.lua compute it with the same operations in the same order, EdBrushTest compares the two and checks smoothness and coherence.

ed_tt_disc(cx, cz, radius, code) paints a hard disc of one terrain type in one call (session grid and sim copy) and returns the changed rectangle;
ed_tt_nodes(x0, z0, nw, nh, step, csx, csz) returns the codes under an overlay node window in one call. Math in EdTerrainTypeMath.h, tested by EdTerrainTypeTest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F37er45a7etRuMgEW1q3kY

